WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.641 --> 00:00:14.683
was staring with wild eyes and trembling from head to foot.

2
00:00:14.703 --> 00:00:17.124
"Heidi, what is going on?"

3
00:00:17.505 --> 00:00:18.425
asked Clara's father.

4
00:00:19.326 --> 00:00:20.486
"Why did you come down here?"

5
00:00:21.407 --> 00:00:26.269
White with terror, and hardly able to speak, Heidi answered, "I don't know."

6
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.652
The doctor quickly stepped in and helped Heidi up to bed.

7
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.080
"Don't be frightened, child.

8
00:00:34.381 --> 00:00:35.961
It's all right," he told her.

9
00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:41.043
The doctor settled Heidi into her bed and stayed with her until she stopped shaking.

10
00:00:41.883 --> 00:00:44.944
Then he asked, "Now tell me, where were you going?"

11
00:00:44.964 --> 00:00:48.505
"Nowhere," answered Heidi.

12
00:00:48.525 --> 00:00:51.786
"I didn't know that I'd gone downstairs.

13
00:00:52.806 --> 00:00:53.746
I was just there."

14
00:00:53.766 --> 00:00:55.587
"Had you been dreaming?"

15
00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.168
"Yes, I dream every night.

16
00:01:00.356 --> 00:01:02.658
I think I am back in Grandfather's hut.

17
00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:08.922
I wonder if the stars are shining, so in my dream I get up and open the door

18
00:01:08.982 --> 00:01:09.503
to the hut.

19
00:01:10.543 --> 00:01:17.528
It's so beautiful, but when I wake up I am still in Frankfurt," said Heidi, struggling to keep

20
00:01:17.588 --> 00:01:18.309
back the tears.

21
00:01:18.329 --> 00:01:22.171
"And where did you live with your Grandfather?"

22
00:01:22.532 --> 00:01:23.252
asked the doctor.

23
00:01:23.272 --> 00:01:31.022
"Up the mountain," said Heidi, "It is beautiful there," and then she broke into violent weeping.

24
00:01:35.185 --> 00:01:37.007
there. Go ahead and cry.

25
00:01:38.188 --> 00:01:39.109
It will do you good.

26
00:01:39.529 --> 00:01:40.170
Don't worry.

27
00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.952
Tomorrow everything will be all right."

28
00:01:43.913 --> 00:01:47.656
The doctor left her quietly and went downstairs to Herr Sesemann.

29
00:01:49.037 --> 00:01:53.161
"First," said the doctor, "let me tell you that Heidi was sleepwalking.

30
00:01:54.242 --> 00:01:56.584
Second, she is consumed by homesickness.

31
00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.561
It looks as if she has lost a lot of weight.

32
00:02:00.522 --> 00:02:01.943
She is practically a skeleton.

33
00:02:02.763 --> 00:02:03.924
There is only one remedy.

34
00:02:04.784 --> 00:02:06.585
You must send her home to her mountain."

35
00:02:08.286 --> 00:02:10.808
Herr Sesemann rose and paced up and down the room.

36
00:02:11.848 --> 00:02:13.469
His face was pale with concern.

37
00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:18.832
The next morning, the maid surprised Heidi by telling her to put on her best clothes.

38
00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:24.856
When Heidi was ready, she went downstairs and found Herr Sesemann and Clara in the study.

39
00:02:25.948 --> 00:02:27.749
"Well, what do you say about this, Heidi?

40
00:02:28.809 --> 00:02:30.550
I've decided that you are going home!"

41
00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:31.851
said Clara's father.

42
00:02:31.871 --> 00:02:36.332
"Home?" Heidi's face turned rosy with delight.

43
00:02:37.493 --> 00:02:38.753
She couldn't believe her ears.

44
00:02:38.773 --> 00:02:42.115
"Oh, yes, yes, home!

45
00:02:42.755 --> 00:02:43.856
I want to go home."

46
00:02:43.876 --> 00:02:49.898
"All right then," said Clara's father, "your carriage is waiting outside.

47
00:02:50.798 --> 00:02:56.064
Say your good-byes to Clara and Sebastian will escort you to Dorfli."

48
00:02:56.084 --> 00:02:58.226
Heidi felt sad about saying good-bye to Clara.

49
00:02:59.247 --> 00:03:03.090
The girls hugged each other, and Clara promised to visit Heidi as soon as she could.

50
00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:08.714
She told Heidi she had filled a small suitcase with dresses and pretty scarves for her.

51
00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:14.779
Then she handed Heidi a basket with 12 fresh rolls for Grannie wrapped in a cloth.

52
00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:21.404
Heidi's delight and sorrow were so evenly mixed that she smiled with tears sparkling in her eyes.

53
00:03:22.548 --> 00:03:27.410
She bundled her favorite book and old straw hat in her red shawl and added them to the

54
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:33.451
basket. Heidi was lifted into the carriage, and Sebastian took his place beside her.

55
00:03:34.592 --> 00:03:39.093
Herr Sesemann lifted her suitcase up beside her and handed Heidi a small thick packet.

56
00:03:39.113 --> 00:03:41.394
"Keep this package safe, Heidi.

57
00:03:42.294 --> 00:03:44.795
It is a present for you and a letter for your grandfather."

58
00:03:45.635 --> 00:03:48.956
Heidi thanked him with all her heart and hid the present in her basket.

59
00:03:50.792 --> 00:03:52.873
Soon, they were on the way to the train station.

60
00:03:53.893 --> 00:03:58.235
Throughout the train ride, Heidi held tightly to her basket with the precious rolls.

61
00:03:59.196 --> 00:04:04.298
The next day, when they got down from the train, the baker from Dorfli was at the station,

62
00:04:04.638 --> 00:04:06.259
loading sacks onto his cart.

63
00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:13.061
Sebastian asked him to take Heidi and her things to Dorfli, and she climbed up onto the seat

64
00:04:13.081 --> 00:04:13.662
of his cart.

65
00:04:14.802 --> 00:04:19.064
As the cart headed up the road, Heidi watched Sebastian waving from behind.

66
00:04:20.105 --> 00:04:23.197
Then she turned to face the mountain, trembling with excitement.
